description:
About Authologic
Authologic.com (YC W21) is a global leader in the full-stack e-ID Hub space. We are supercharging the current OCR/liveness KYC stack by supporting identity wallets, bank IDs, government-issued digital IDs, and more. We are a fast-growing, Series A startup spanning Silicon Valley, the UK, and the EU.
About the role
Authologic is building digital identity infrastructure at the intersection of the most impactful EU regulations: eIDAS 2.0, PSD3/PSR, AML/CFT, DORA and the AI Act.
We operate close to the source of regulatory change -- not just reacting to it, but actively shaping how new frameworks are understood and implemented in practice. This makes our position on the market genuinely unique.
You will be joining a fast-growing company at the right stage -- where key decisions are still being made, and your impact is real.
We are looking for someone who doesn't just interpret regulations, but understands how they translate into real products, user flows and business decisions.
Who we're looking for:
A regulatory/compliance professional who:
thinks independently and can draw well-reasoned conclusions;
is well-organised and able to manage multiple workstreams;
is comfortable working close to product, tech and business teams;
understands how regulation impacts real-life implementation;
Must have:
strong, hands-on experience in AML/CFT, in particular:
developing and implementing AML procedures and methodologies;
applying customer due diligence (CDD) / enhanced due diligence (EDD) measures;
practical understanding of financial security measures and risk-based approach;
solid knowledge of:
PSD2 / PSD3 / PSR;
DORA;
AI Act;
general understanding of:
trust services and the digital identity ecosystem;
the direction of eIDAS 2.0 (you don't need to know it inside out -- it's new, but you need to understand what it is about);
min. 3 years of experience in:
a financial institution, or
regulatory advisory (law firm / consultancy), or
payment institution / fintech;
ability to work hands-on, not only at a theoretical level;
strong analytical skills and ability to connect regulatory dots;
professional proficiency in Polish (required);
business/legal proficiency in English.
Nice to have:
experience as AMLRO / MLRO;
experience with:
digital identity / KYC / onboarding
authentication / SCA
cross-border regulatory projects
Formal qualification:
legal qualifications (attorney-at-law / advocate) are not required.
Why join:
a unique position on the market, operating at the forefront of regulatory change;
join a fast-growing company at the right stage (real impact, not corporate inertia);
real impact on product and business decisions;
high ownership and autonomy;
a team that treats regulation as a strategic advantage, not a constraint.
GDPR Clause
I hereby consent to the processing of personal data contained in my application to be processed by Authologic Sp. z o.o. I hereby also give consent for personal data included in my CV to be processed for the purposes of any future recruitment process.
